  "result": "Perfect! All 221 tests pass. Here's the summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\n**New file: `src/credits.js`**\n- `createCreditNote(invoice, { amount, reason, date }, existingNumbers)` function that creates refund credit notes\n  - Returns ok(creditNote) with: { number, invoiceNumber, customerId, amount, reason, date }\n  - Validates invoice is issued, partially_paid, or paid (NOT_ISSUED error for draft)\n  - Validates amount is a positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID error)\n  - Validates amount doesn't exceed invoice total (CREDIT_TOO_HIGH error)\n  - Generates credit note number with CN prefix: CN-YYYY-NNNN\n  - Separate counter from invoices, but handles both in existingNumbers array\n\n**New test file: `test/credits.test.js`**\n- 19 comprehensive tests covering:\n  - Draft invoice rejection\n  - Amount validation (negative, zero, non-integer rejection)\n  - Overpayment detection\n  - Valid credit note creation\n  - CN number format and sequencing\n  - Counter increment for same year\n  - Counter reset for new year\n  - Support for issued, partially_paid, and paid invoices\n  - Mixed invoice and credit note number handling\n  - Reason text preservation\n  - Date handling\n  - Edge cases and boundary conditions\n\n**Updated `src/errors.js`**\n- Added `CREDIT_TOO_HIGH` error code\n\n**Updated `HANDOFF.md`**\n- Documented createCreditNote function and usage\n- Added CREDIT_TOO_HIGH to error codes\n- Updated test counts (221 total)\n- Added credit notes implementation notes\n\nAll 221 tests pass \u2713",
